[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded resistor temperature coefficients

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Acceptance target: unchanged original regression/temper/temper-res-1.cir,
all ten requested Celsius points, six root voltage/current observables,
original three errors and success assertion against stock ngspice, without
weaker tolerances. Reuse the existing generated resistor metadata,
ParameterEvaluator, requested per-temperature circuit compilation, and bounded
reporting expression evaluator. This is a small extension of the adopted
resistor lowering, not a new numerical subsystem or replacement interpreter.
The retained reuse assessment docs/spicesharp-evaluation.md records the user's
Rust/public-API decision and candidate limitations. No dependency is added.
Pinned RSpice model_resolution/resistors.rs defines instance-over-model TC1,
TC2 and TCE, and TCE precedence. Its implementation is behavioral guidance;
no source is copied. Complete independent stock-ngspice execution is required.

Plan: reproduce original refusal; add failing per-point effective-resistance,
coefficient precedence/domain and textual condition regressions; implement
finite positive multiplier preparation and generated control-only word aliases;
replay unchanged original; collect full managed regression/coverage, reproducible
properties, malformed-input tests, mutation and real StrictDoc evidence.
Temperature increments are Celsius differences, numerically equal to kelvin
differences. The default nominal temperature is 27 C; only explicit model TNOM
is admitted additionally. Instance TEMP/DTEMP, higher coefficients and arbitrary
physical directive settings remain outside this bounded profile.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-RESISTOR-TEMPERATURE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Requested resistor temperature coefficients
STATEMENT: >>>
Requested resistor preparation shall apply TC1 and TC2 as a polynomial in
simulation temperature minus model nominal temperature, using a default nominal
temperature of 27 C. Explicit TCE shall override that polynomial and use
1.01 raised to TCE times the temperature difference. Instance coefficients
shall independently override model coefficients. A nonfinite or nonpositive
multiplier or effective resistance shall refuse atomically. Invalid multipliers
shall identify invalid_resistor_temperature_factor, preserving failure provenance
separately from invalid nominal or effective resistance. The original
resistor source ranges, geometry, scalar precedence, scaling and multiplicity
contracts shall be retained. Strict non-requested profiles shall not silently
admit these additional physical settings.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ResistorModelLowering.PrepareRequested and OperatingPointBridge.
Verification: ResistorTemperatureTests; unchanged original temper-res-1.cir.
Evidence: evidence/resistor-temperature.json and docs/resistor-temperature-results.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-WORD-BOOLEAN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Generated textual boolean aliases
STATEMENT: >>>
The control-only generated expression lexer shall recognize case-insensitive
AND and OR as the existing conjunction and disjunction operators, with existing
precedence and finite real vector rules. Ordinary deck identifiers shall remain
available with those spellings. Reporting shall evaluate the complete original
assertions and preserve failures rather than interpreting them as agreement.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Grammar/SpiceLexer.g4 and ControlVectorExecution.Binary.
Verification: WordBooleanTests and complete original temper-res reporting.
Evidence: evidence/resistor-temperature.json.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CONTROL-REAL-POWER-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Finite real reporting exponentiation
STATEMENT: >>>
The existing reporting expression tree shall evaluate ^ and ** for finite real
operands, retaining scalar broadcasting and vector shape rules. Nonreal inputs
and nonfinite power results shall refuse explicitly. This shall use the standard
Math.Pow implementation and existing finite result validation, without a second
expression parser or a new numerical dependency.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ControlVectorExecution.Binary; verification: WordBooleanTests.
Evidence: evidence/resistor-temperature.json; no complex-power claim.
<<<
